ollama_content:
{'translated_term': '\u04e0\u0438\u0431\u0430\u0442\u043c\u0438\u0443\u0449 \u0441\u043e\u0446\u043b\u044f\u043b\u044f\u0441\u044c\u0441\u043a \u0441\u0430\u043c\u044b\u0440\u0442\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0449', 
 'translation_rationale': 'The term "Computational Social Science" can be broken down into its constituent parts. "\u04e0\u0438\u0431\u0430\u0442\u043c\u0438\u0443\u0449" refers to the field of study itself, while "\u0440\u0438\u0444 \u0441\u043e\u0446\u043b\u044a\u043b\u0445\u0441\u044l\u044f\u0441\u044c\u0441k\u0438\u0449" means a science that uses computations. The suffix "-skii" in Avaric is used to form nouns denoting sciences or fields of study, similar to Latin-derived languages such as English and French.'}

Alternative translation:
{'translated_term': '\u04e0\u0438\u0431 \u0444\u044f\u043b\u0441\u0442\u044a\u044c\u0445\u0439 \u0441\u043e\u0446\u043b\u0442\u044f\u0443\u0442\u044f \u0440\u0438\u0444 \u0441\u043e\u0446\u043b\u0445\u0447\u0438\u0443', 
 'translation_rationale': This translation emphasizes the computational aspect of social science, using the word "\u04e0\u0438\u0431" to mean "science" and "\u0444\u044f\u043b\u0441\u0442\u044a\u044c\u0445\u0439" to mean "computational". The phrase "\u0441\u043o\u0446\u043f\u0440\u044e\u0443\u0442\u0443" means "social science", while the suffix "-skii" forms a noun denoting the field of study.'}

{'translated_term': 'Kallon Kajij Erikoj Sosiojik', 'translation_rationale': 'I used "Kallon" (meaning "science") and "Erikoj Sosiojik" (meaning "computational social science") to convey the meaning of "Computational Social Science". This combination is inspired by Marshallese phrases, where "-ion" is a suffix often added to words to create nouns or technical terms. The term "Killon Kajij Erikoj Sosiojik" could also be interpreted as "Social Science with Calculations", which better aligns with the computational aspect of the field.'}

Alternatively, if I were to use more literal translation:

{'translated_term': 'Erikoj Kallen Sosiojik', 'translation_rationale': 'Using this term, "Kallen" (meaning "science") is paired with "Erikoj" (meaning "computational"), which could be a bit awkward in Marshallese pronunciation. However, it clearly conveys the meaning of the term.'}

Note that Marshallese language and grammar may vary across different regions or dialects, so these translations are intended to serve as a starting point for further refinement and evaluation.

{'translated_term': 'Орныг Угсрын Хуудал' , 'translation_rationale': 'In Mongolian, "орныг" (ᠠᠷᠩᠭ) means "science" or "research," while "угсрын" (ᠤᠬᠰᠳᠨ) implies "computation" or "calculation." "Хуудал" (ᠬᠮᠳᠠᠯ) means "study" or "research." This translation aims to convey the idea of computational methods applied to social sciences.'}

Alternative translations:

{'translated_term': 'Давсныл Хэвэлэн' , 'translation_rationale': A possible alternative is "Давсныл Хэвэлэн" (ᠳᠣᠭᠰᠨᠡᠪ ᠬᠢᠫᠤ), which combines "дава" (ᠳᠣᠰ) meaning "science," "сныл" (ᠰᠨᠡᠬ) implying "computing" or "calculating," and "хэвэлэн" (ᠬᠢᠪ) meaning "research" or "study."

{'translated_term': 'Vipassanīya Sāsamajik Aṅgavijjā', 
 'translation_rationale': 'This term roughly translates to "Insightful Social Analysis" or "Analytical Study of Social Phenomena". The word Vipassanīya (meaning "insight" or "wisdom") is inspired by the Buddhist concept of vipassanā, which emphasizes direct perception and understanding. Sāsamajik refers to social or society-related topics, while Aṅgavijjā means "analysis" or " investigation". This translation captures the essence of Computational Social Science as a field that employs analytical methods to study complex social phenomena.', 
 'alternatives': [
  {'term': 'Sāsana Sāsamajik Vijjā', 'rationale': 'This term roughly translates to "Religious Social Analysis" or "Sacred Study of Society". However, this translation may not fully capture the computational and analytical aspects of Computational Social Science.'}, 
  {'term': 'Dhamma Sāsana Aṅgavijjā', 'rationale': 'This term roughly translates to "Buddhist Teaching Social Analysis" or "Study of Society in Accordance with Dhamma". While this translation maintains a connection to Buddhist thought, it may not convey the full scope and methodology of Computational Social Science.'}
]}

{'translated_term': 'Computasionele Sociale Wetenschappen', 
 'translation_rationale': 'Ik heb "Computasionele" gekozen als voorvoegsel om de focus op computermacht en -technologie te benadrukken. Sociale Wetenschappen is een Nederlandse term die het veld breed omschrijft, waarin computational social science onderdeel kan zijn van de sociale wetenschap. Het is echter ook nodig om te voorkomen dat de term "wetenschappelijk" wordt geassocieerd met de natuurwetenschappen. Alternatieve voorvoegselsopties zijn "sociale" of "computasionale", maar "computasionele" lijkt me het meest correcte keuze.', 
 'alternative_terms': ['Sociale Wetenschappen', 'Computasionale Wetenschap']}

