{'translated_term': 'Cisab Ayyuntiinô Misso Êndawwâtiyo', 
'translation_rationale': 'I translated "Computational Social Science" into Afar by breaking it down into its core components. "Cisab Ayyuntiinô" translates to "social science" in Afar, as "ci-saba" means "science" and "ayyuntii" conveys social or relational aspects. The addition of "Misso" suggests a focus on methodology or approach, which is characteristic of computational social science. Finally, adding the suffix "-Êndawwâtiyo" indicates a connection to technology or computation, which is essential to the field. 
